# RFC 5321 requires postmaster to be reachable, the zone CAA record names
# hostmaster for incident reports, and abuse is expected by every reputation
# service. All three were accepted at SMTP and then TempFailed on delivery,
# because with a wildcard the maildir action expands %{dest.user} to the
# ORIGINAL localpart -- /home/hostmaster/Maildir -- not to the mapped user.
# Explicit entries expand to the user they name.
postmaster@brgen.no    johann
hostmaster@brgen.no    johann
abuse@brgen.no         johann
dmarc@brgen.no         johann

# Anything else at the domain. Safe now that the maildir path resolves from the
# MAPPED user rather than the recipient localpart.
@brgen.no              johann
